      "readme": "Resting state fMRI data acquired on a cohort of triple transgenic mice for Alzheimer's disease-like pathology, 3xTGAD, and a cohort of controls. \nAim: to investigate the changes in resting-state network organization within the brain during pathology progression, in a preclinical setting. \nAnimals underwent scanning session at two time-points: 3 and 6 months of age.\n\nOne mouse presented hydrocephalic condition.\n",
